  "description": "Installation of an internally illuminated digital display.",
  "development_type": "Other advertisements",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "No advertisement is to be displayed without the permission of the owner of the site or any other person with an interest in the site entitled to grant permission.\r\rReason: This is a standard condition required by Regulation 14(1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) Regulations 2007.",
    "No advertisement shall be sited or displayed so as to(a) endanger persons using any highway, railway, waterway, dock, harbour or aerodrome (civil or military);(b) obscure, or hinder the ready interpretation of, any traffic sign, railway signal or aid to navigation by water or air:(c) hinder the operation of any device used for the purpose of security or surveillance or for the measuring of the speed of any vehicle. \r\rReason: This is a standard condition required by Regulation 14(1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) Regulations 2007.",
    "Any advertisements displayed, and any site used for the display of advertisements, shall be maintained in a condition that does not impair the visual amenity of the site.\r\rReason: This is a standard condition required by Regulation 14(1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) Regulations 2007.",
    "Any structure or hoarding erected or used principally for the purpose of displaying advertisements shall be maintained in a condition that does not endanger the public.\r\rReason: This is a standard condition required by Regulation 14(1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) Regulations 2007.",
    "Where an advertisement is required under these Regulations to be removed, the site shall be left in a condition that does not endanger the public or impair visual amenity.\r\rReason: This is a standard condition required by Regulation 14(1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) Regulations 2007.",
    "The display of this advertisement(s) is valid for a period of 5 years from the date of this consent. \r\rReason: This is a standard condition required by Regulation 14(1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning (Control of Advertisements) Regulations 2007.",
    "The maximum luminance of the digital display screens hereby approved shall be automatically controlled and shall not exceed 5000 cd/m2 during daylight hours, and shall be automatically dimmed to a maximum of 600 cd/m2 between dusk and dawn. The operational illumination levels must strictly adhere to the standards and boundaries set for this size and type of screen by the Institute of Lighting Professionals, within Professional Lighting Guide 05 (The Brightness of Illuminated Advertisements), or any subsequent superseding guidance.  \r\rReason: To safeguard the visual amenities of the surrounding streetscene, prevent intrusive light pollution, and ensure the display does not create a visual hazard to pedestrian or highway safety, in accordance with Policies 28, 29 and 36 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018)."
  ],
